<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Orange Free State Province</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1910">1910</a>–<a href="/years/1994">1994</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Orange Free State Province was one of the four provinces of the Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> and later the Republic of South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, formed in 1910 from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orange-river-colony">Orange River Colony</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bloemfontein">Bloemfontein</a> as its capital. It kept the borders of the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> republic, and in 1994 it became the Free State province.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/orange-free-state-province.jpg" alt="Orange Free State Province" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Benbennick wrote this file · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Orange_Free_State.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
